1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,339
Personnel shows a member’s
roles separately from staffing,

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:05,199
status, and administrative state.

3
00:00:05,599 --> 00:00:09,470
In our fictional Chicago Fire
department, Casey begins with Officer,

4
00:00:09,689 --> 00:00:12,229
On Shift, Standing By, and Admin.

5
00:00:12,779 --> 00:00:15,229
Choose Manage Roles to
inspect the catalog.

6
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,700
The page lists each role’s
description and member count.

7
00:00:19,049 --> 00:00:22,530
It also explains how role order
chooses an available custom

8
00:00:22,569 --> 00:00:24,350
icon for a person’s map pin.

9
00:00:24,809 --> 00:00:29,100
We will leave the original six roles
and their order unchanged, and add one

10
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,340
clearly marked coordination exercise.

11
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:32,870
Choose Add Role.

12
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:37,349
Enter Training Only, Community
Response Navigator as the Name.

13
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:41,599
Use the Description to explain the
fictional community paramedicine and

14
00:00:41,599 --> 00:00:43,610
mental health coordination exercise.

15
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:47,150
Our description explicitly
separates software training from

16
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:50,690
professional qualification and
system administration privileges.

17
00:00:51,019 --> 00:00:53,729
Custom icon is optional and remains empty.

18
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:57,849
A useful role name tells another
administrator what the role is for;

19
00:00:58,229 --> 00:01:02,540
its description explains the intended
scope before anyone is assigned to it.

20
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:06,150
The lower form previews the
default icon on light and dark

21
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:07,839
backgrounds and in a list.

22
00:01:08,259 --> 00:01:10,180
No custom file has been selected.

23
00:01:10,649 --> 00:01:14,049
Use Save, then find the new
role at the end of the catalog.

24
00:01:14,509 --> 00:01:19,379
Users In Role is zero, and the original
six rows retain their order and counts.

25
00:01:19,769 --> 00:01:23,660
Choose View on the new row to read
its stored name and full description.

26
00:01:24,109 --> 00:01:26,959
Creating the role has given
us a saved definition, but

27
00:01:26,959 --> 00:01:28,480
has not yet assigned a member.

28
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:32,330
From the new role’s row,
open Required certifications.

29
00:01:32,739 --> 00:01:36,449
The notice says enforcement
is Off, and Member eligibility

30
00:01:36,449 --> 00:01:38,259
says the role has no members.

31
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:40,369
Add requirement creates a row.

32
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:45,289
Select the fictional record-review
type, check Mandatory, leave Any-of

33
00:01:45,289 --> 00:01:50,560
group blank, leave Allow trainee clear,
and enter seven for Grace override.

34
00:01:50,959 --> 00:01:54,609
Save, then reopen the page
and read the same single row.

35
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:58,379
The seven-day setting concerns
the removal grace calculation if

36
00:01:58,379 --> 00:02:02,759
enforcement applies; it does not
change a certification record’s expiry.

37
00:02:02,919 --> 00:02:06,409
Choose Certification types to
verify the full identity behind

38
00:02:06,409 --> 00:02:08,130
the narrow requirement selector.

39
00:02:08,530 --> 00:02:12,020
The training review row shows
its complete code, one existing

40
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:14,270
record, and now one requirement.

41
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:15,869
Open its Edit control.

42
00:02:16,289 --> 00:02:19,240
Code is read-only, and the
help explains that a role

43
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:21,170
requirement references this type.

44
00:02:21,609 --> 00:02:25,660
Applies to remains locked at Person
because a record already uses it.

45
00:02:25,990 --> 00:02:27,920
We are inspecting these fields only.

46
00:02:28,209 --> 00:02:30,929
Keep the existing record
and type settings intact.

47
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:35,040
Back on the role’s requirements
page, add a second, distinct

48
00:02:35,040 --> 00:02:37,040
type for an unsaved comparison.

49
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:40,640
With both Mandatory boxes
checked and both group fields

50
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:44,640
blank, the rows express separate
requirements: both would be needed.

51
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:48,640
Give both rows group number one,
and they become alternatives:

52
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,640
either could satisfy that group.

53
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:54,240
This is a form preview, so do not Save.

54
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:58,640
Reloading restores the original single
row, blank group, and seven-day override.

55
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:02,240
Saving would replace the stored
requirement set; the discarded

56
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:04,240
preview changes none of it.

57
00:03:04,299 --> 00:03:08,740
To assign the role, return to
Personnel and use Edit on Casey’s row.

58
00:03:09,109 --> 00:03:13,639
In the profile’s Roles field, wait for
the existing Officer selection to load.

59
00:03:13,990 --> 00:03:16,660
It must remain selected
when adding another role.

60
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:22,059
Group is Truck 81 and Is Group Admin
is already checked in this fictional

61
00:03:22,059 --> 00:03:24,270
account; leave both unchanged.

62
00:03:24,690 --> 00:03:28,100
This page contains other profile
settings, so keep the exercise

63
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:31,889
focused on the intended additional
role rather than changing membership,

64
00:03:32,049 --> 00:03:34,160
contact, or administrative options.

65
00:03:34,279 --> 00:03:37,630
Use the profile’s Roles selector
for the additional assignment.

66
00:03:38,069 --> 00:03:41,939
Community is entered in the lookup,
while Officer remains selected.

67
00:03:42,359 --> 00:03:45,500
The prepared selection then
contains two complete chips:

68
00:03:45,859 --> 00:03:50,229
Officer and the new Training Only,
Community Response Navigator role.

69
00:03:50,699 --> 00:03:52,549
Read both names before saving.

70
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,629
This control submits the whole selected
role set, so an existing role must remain

71
00:03:57,629 --> 00:03:59,500
present if you intend to preserve it.

72
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:03,610
Adding the new chip is preparation;
we still need a saved readback.

73
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,480
Before saving, compare the
unchanged profile controls.

74
00:04:07,849 --> 00:04:11,449
Department Admin is already
selected, while Disable User

75
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:13,069
and Hide User are clear.

76
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:14,380
We leave them that way.

77
00:04:14,789 --> 00:04:16,529
Use the normal Save once.

78
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:19,680
Back in Personnel,
search for Matthew Casey.

79
00:04:20,069 --> 00:04:24,149
His row now lists Officer and the
new coordination role together.

80
00:04:24,459 --> 00:04:28,489
Staffing remains On Shift,
status remains Standing By, and

81
00:04:28,489 --> 00:04:30,780
administrative state still reads Admin.

82
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:35,250
The result is an additional operational
role on the same member, not a

83
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:37,209
new staffing or status selection.

84
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:40,960
Use the member’s Edit control
again to check persistence.

85
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:44,560
Both role chips are present
in the fresh profile.

86
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:48,560
Truck 81 remains selected and
Is Group Admin remains checked.

87
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:52,160
Farther down, Department Admin
is still selected, while Disable

88
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:54,560
User and Hide User remain clear.

89
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,560
This second visit is read-only.

90
00:04:56,560 --> 00:05:01,360
Verify the particular fields involved in
your exercise instead of assuming that

91
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:04,160
a typed or selected value was stored.

92
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:06,960
Keep unrelated profile and
permission choices unchanged.

93
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:08,560
Return through Manage Roles.

94
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:11,360
The new role now has one member.

95
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:16,160
Choose its View control to see Casey
listed under the stored description.

96
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:20,560
Open Required certifications from that
role’s row to inspect Member eligibility.

97
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:24,560
Casey is marked Qualified for this
single fictional software rule.

98
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:28,560
The Off notice remains visible:
this result does not demonstrate

99
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:30,160
enforcement blocking or removal.

100
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:34,960
Read the rule, the member, and the
software result together, and keep

101
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,760
professional authorization decisions
outside this training exercise.

102
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:42,560
Chicago Fire can use this workflow to
describe an exercise coordination role.

103
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:46,160
Community care and mental health
teams can organize operational

104
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,760
responsibilities without patient detail.

105
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:51,760
Search and rescue can distinguish
search and support roles; security

106
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:55,760
teams can define site responsibilities;
wildland teams can organize seasonal

107
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:58,960
coordination; and industrial
response teams can separate staff

108
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,560
functions from equipment inspections.

109
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:03,360
In each setting, use clear
descriptions, deliberate

110
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:04,960
requirements, and verified membership.

111
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:08,160
Preserve existing assignments and
administrative settings, and check

112
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:10,560
saved results before relying on them.

